 body='<div class="kicker">Append-only session reconciliation · 7 October 2026</div><h1>Discoveries and corrections.</h1><p class="lead">Architecture development is now catalogued alongside the unchanged code-review release0.5. New evidence is scoped to its own mathematical and computational contract.</p>'
 changes=[('Launch moments widen the conditional window eightfold','EXACT: in the source frame, Hψ₀=p1 and H²ψ₀=p0+p2. These conserve unit first-generator norm and yield the cold allowance7w/1024+w². DERIVED conditional retained error &lt;127/2²³&lt;2⁻¹⁶ throughout16±2⁻¹¹ at unchangedβ=5/16. The separate curvature route selects the same dyadic candidate; nine propagation controls and seventeen integer decisions pass. No numerical continuum derivative transfer or physical promotion follows.'),('Fourfold conditional retention window','DERIVED: retained dyad charge64→14 by bath partial-trace cancellation and low-excitation coupling norms. The finite192-mode derivative certificate &lt;2⁻²⁰ plus uniform continuum value comparisons yields retained error &lt;31/2²¹&lt;2⁻¹⁶ throughout16±2⁻¹⁴ model time units, at unchangedβ=5/16. Numerical continuum derivative transfer remains OPEN. The failed61/2²² display ceiling and post-evaluation reporting clarification are preserved; the acceptance target was unchanged. <a href="/research/MQM_RESPONSE_JET_v0.1/JET_REVIEW_ADDENDUM.md">Supplementary review gatesR13–R16</a>. External review unperformed; physical promotion0.'),('Uniform finite retention window','DERIVED conditional error below15/2²⁰&lt;2⁻¹⁶ throughout16±2⁻¹⁶ at unchangedβ=5/16. Local cold-population flow, noncommuting second-order continuity and uniform Gaussian remainder are separately charged. This gives2⁻¹⁶ post-deadline model-time hold; the equal-valued error threshold is a different typed quantity. The wider declared dyadic control has an insufficient bound, not a physical failure result.'),('External-review handoff prepared','Six dependency bundles with hashes,12 ordered review gates and a blank reviewer response ledger are included. No reviewer contacted or independent review performed. <a href="/research/MQM_RETENTION_WINDOW_v0.1/EXTERNAL_REVIEW_PACKET.md">Review handoff</a>. Physical promotion remains0.'),('Conditional thermal acceptance at the frozen temperature','DERIVED: directed quadrature intervals,128 degree48 Taylor steps, and explicit roundoff allowances give retained error below773/2²⁶+2⁻¹²⁸&lt;2⁻¹⁶ at β=5/16,T=16. The certificate assumes the declared arithmetic model and inherited continuum/Gaussian bounds. External review, permanent retention, physical implementation and arbitrary-input diamond error remain OPEN. The initial Decimal-context repair is preserved.'),('Source-bound spectral reference, separately typed','EXACT: on the15-coordinate tetrahedral operator, the zero projector has rank1 and the oriented positive-frequency projector rank7. Their sum defines a proposed rank8 carrier with unique zero reference. This post-exposure construction does not identifyTheta, derive uniform allocation, divide by24 or4, or establish7/768 as a material constant. <a href="/research/MQM_DIRECTED_RESPONSE_v0.1/AUDIT_NOTES.md">Audit assumptions</a>.'),('Centered transfer closes the ideal-size mismatch','DERIVED: the time-centered bath embedding gives a fixed-launch second-order vacuum allowance below2⁻³⁰ at M192. Eight supplementary numerical embedding controls pass; these are not directed certificates. The full2⁻¹⁶ thermal target remains OPEN pending directed finite-response error.'),('Capacity provenance and selection gates','EXACT arithmetic7/768=(2³−1)/(4·4!·2³), with intermediate7/192. The packet carrier remains15 coordinates and28 incidences. A rank7 diagonal selector is excluded only in the stated left-regular S4 ansatz; a coherent rank7 example exists but does not derive source selection or allocation. Reference configuration, extra4 admissibility law and latch map remain OPEN. <a href="/research/MQM_CENTERED_TRANSFER_v0.1/CAPACITY_SELECTION_GATES.md">Selection ledger</a>.'),('Full finite thermal response and sharper transfer','SIMULATED: all covariance-weighted columns at32,64,128,192 modes are now evaluated; M192 response is2.2506×10⁻⁸. A DERIVED Chebyshev allowance &lt;2⁻²²⁹ at L1536 halves the previous sufficient site count. A separate exact covariance comparison at192 Gauss nodes is &lt;2⁻⁵⁷ in the response ledger. Vacuum transfer at192 and directed numerical error remain OPEN. The cold diagnostic repair and after-evaluation proof additions are disclosed in the new package.'),('Local-drive transfer allowance clears','DERIVED / exact arithmetic. Keeping β=5/16 and T=16, retain exact continuum thermal covariance and truncate only vacuum propagation. L=3072 yields δchain,2&lt;2⁻⁴⁵¹. The full second-order thermal response remains OPEN.'),('Second-order identity and sparse reference','Finite regularizations admit the covariance-weighted Q=2 identity after subtracting vacuum normalization. Individual continuum trN terms cannot be promoted separately. Sparse M768 assembly is checked; full response propagation is not complete.'),('Frequency resolution narrows thermal debit','The conditional thermal ceiling is below2⁻¹³ at original temperature. Gaussian corrections of fourth and higher order are below2⁻²⁵. The remaining second-order sufficient budget is127/2²⁵−2⁻¹²⁸.'),('Cold continuum bridge','Legendre mapping and directed cold-reference enclosure give q∞(16)&lt;3/262144+2⁻¹²⁸. This is point-time vacuum capture, not permanent hold or thermal operation.'),('Admission and compiler obstructions remain scoped','Single-native admission has exact constructions; six-qubit joint admission remains open. Moment matching alone is insufficient. Candidate exclusions, charge-family restrictions and graph witnesses are not universal two-local no-go theorems.'),('Capacity and material proposals repaired','The7/768 threshold is source-defined, not an intrinsic graphene transport law. Graphene transmission models need specified boundaries and calibrated parameters; analogy to gravitational capacity is not a physical derivation. A local dissipator does not itself close high-weight completion gating or reservoir engineering.')]
