 body+=section('Corrections that constrain every later claim','<ul><li>The earlier short-step2⁻³² vector and2⁻⁴³ response allowances describe an ideal exact-arithmetic design; directed numerical implementation remains open.</li><li>The0.029003 midpoint transfer majorant is insufficient, not a physical error floor. The newer chain proof uses a different reference and more sites.</li><li>Finite photon tails apply to K≤1 or K≤2 truncations, respectively; they are not uniform infinite-volume Fock bounds.</li><li>Dark-state projector commutation alone does not guarantee stored-data preservation. A declared storage generator and reverse-jump ledger are required.</li><li>The displayed two-qubit latch Hamiltonian is a controlled-X term, not an XY exchange. Two-local effective jump support does not automatically establish two-body system–reservoir implementation.</li><li>Copper-12 is not a valid copper isotope designation; no such heat-sink or universal emitted-energy lower bound is promoted.</li><li>No universal12.5% reflection floor, CAP accuracy, clock compression advantage, or hardware noise screening is established by an unverified synopsis.</li><li>A conservative-bound failure does not prove cooling necessary. Physical promotion remains0.</li></ul>')
